Z||000004||DRA||06-23-2000||08:23 AM||||Tread pattern looks more like a touring type tire, not very aggressive tread. Took a spin around last night in wet conditions, they'll do till I can get the 17in wheels and dunlop W2's. Thanks for the replys guys!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Zman302||06-24-2000||02:32 AM||||the grand am tires are pretty good tires.  they sell them across the river in ohio.  Had a set on my camaro.  The problem i had with them was they seemed to be a bit hard.  I would burn the tires off at every light(16 and 68 camaro don't mix well) and the tires wouldnt wear out.  They were terrible in the rain too, if the road was even damp they would go up in smoke.  The good thing is you shouldnt need tires for a long time.||||reg||1
Z||000006||batboy||06-24-2000||09:21 AM||||Certainly a far cry from BFG Comp T/A's which are damn good tires. Most of those cheapie off brands are designed for maximum wear, so they use a hard compound to get ol' farts to bragb about how they got 85,000 miles out of their last set of tires. We all know that with sports cars and for performance driving, you need a softer tread compound so the tire sticks like glue to the road.||||reg||1
